{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/memberindices"]}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The stored column of either plane, read in place: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MemberIndices"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix","preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule0aB0V","text":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule0aB0V13MemberIndicesV","text":"MemberIndices"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","symbolKind":"typealias","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MemberIndices","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L200"},"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MemberIndices"}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices","roleHeading":"Type Alias","externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V13MemberIndicesa"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/MemberIndices":{"title":"IncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The indices of the set bits of one stored row, ascending, read in place: a column’s member","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indices, or a vertex’s column indices (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidentHyperedgeIndices"},{"text":"). No copy and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allocation, unlike a ","type":"text"},{"code":"BitSet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It shares the matrix’s words copy-on-write, so a later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mutation of the matrix leaves it unchanged.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MemberIndices","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix\/memberindices","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MemberIndices","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","abstract":[{"text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of column ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedHypergraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hypergraphs","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"type":"topic","title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule":{"title":"IncidenceMatrixModule","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/IncidenceMatrix","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceMatrix"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The unoriented incidence matrix of a hypergraph: an n × m matrix of bits with cell (v, p) set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":" is a member of column "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":". The vertices are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" and the columns,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the hyperedges, are at positions "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<hyperedgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" algorithms run on it unchanged; it is not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" even when built from one,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"because a cell edit can give a column any number of bits."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceMatrix"}],"type":"topic","title":"IncidenceMatrix"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/MemberIndices":{"fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MemberIndices","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The stored column of either plane, read in place: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix.MemberIndices"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/MemberIndices","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/memberindices","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MemberIndices","kind":"identifier"}]}}}